  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 16 files needed for the S3 authentication security audit of Ceph RGW, in priority order:\n\n**Core signature verification (V2/V4)**\n- `src/rgw/rgw_auth_s3.cc` / `.h` \u2014 implements `get_v4_signature`, `get_v2_signature`, `parse_v4_credentials`, `is_time_skew_ok` (the `RGW_AUTH_GRACE` = 15-min replay window), canonical request/string-to-sign construction, and the AWSv4 chunked-upload signature verification (`AWSv4ComplMulti`/`AWSv4ComplSingle`)\n- `src/rgw/rgw_rest_s3.cc` / `.h` \u2014 `RGW_Auth_S3::authorize`, `AWSGeneralAbstractor::get_auth_data_v2/v4` (where V2 vs V4 selection/fallback happens), `LocalEngine::authenticate`, `AWSSignerV4`\n\n**Auth framework**\n- `src/rgw/rgw_auth.h` / `.cc` \u2014 `Engine`, `Strategy`, `IdentityApplier`, `Completer` base classes and the strategy chaining/fallback logic\n- `src/rgw/rgw_auth_registry.h` \u2014 strategy registry wiring V2/V4/anonymous engines together\n- `src/rgw/rgw_auth_filters.h` \u2014 auth decorator filters\n\n**Secret key storage/access**\n- `src/rgw/rgw_common.h` / `.cc` \u2014 `RGWUserInfo`, credential structures\n- `src/rgw/driver/rados/rgw_zone.cc` \u2014 `RGWAccessKey` definition (access key ID + secret key pairing)\n\n**Supporting**\n- `src/rgw/rgw_rest.h` / `.cc` \u2014 REST handler dispatch, header extraction\n- `src/rgw/rgw_crypt_sanitize.h` \u2014 log redaction of secrets (relevant to secret-key exposure checks)\n- `src/common/ceph_crypto.h` / `.cc` \u2014 the underlying HMAC-SHA1/SHA256 primitives used for signing, relevant to checking whether signature comparison is constant-time",
